  "title": "ConceptService.saveDrug Impact in REST Module",
  "updatedAt": 1793523097446,
  "answers": [
    {
      "id": "3iSaZ0F3R6pfDwsd",
      "productId": "openmrs",
      "question": "If the behaviour of `ConceptService.saveDrug` in openmrs-core changed, which code in the REST web services module (openmrs-module-webservices.rest) uses it and could be affected?",
      "generation": "g-b59a21",
      "kind": "partial",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "`ConceptService.saveDrug` is declared on the service interface [1] and implemented as a thin wrapper that checks the global-property lock and delegates to the DAO [2]; the DAO does a Hibernate `saveOrUpdate` [3]. So a behaviour change would surface wherever something in webservices.rest writes a `Drug` through that call — mainly the `1.8`/`1.10`/`1.11`/`1.12` `Drug` resources and the `DrugIngredient`/`DrugReferenceMap` sub-resources that persist the parent drug.",
          "citations": [
            1,
            2,
            3
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Confirmed affected (direct calls in scope)**",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- `DrugResource1_8.save()` — the core drug CRUD write path; it calls `saveDrug` and returns the saved object, so the POST/PUT response body is directly affected [4]. `DrugResource1_10`, `DrugResource1_11` and `DrugResource1_12` all extend it indirectly [5], [6], and they are the resources registered for `/drug` on newer Core versions [7], so the inherited `save()` is the one serving `/ws/rest/v1/drug`.\n- `DrugIngredientResource1_11.save()` — adds the ingredient to the parent drug and then calls `saveDrug` on that parent [8]. Because the `1.11`/`1.12` drug resources expose `ingredients` via a property setter [9], the same write can also flow through a plain drug create/update, not only the sub-resource.\n- `DrugIngredientResource1_11.purge()` — detaches the ingredient and persists the parent drug again [10].\n- `DrugReferenceMapResource1_10.save()` — adds the map to the drug then persists it [11]; registered for `/drugreferencemap` [12].\n- Tests that assert write behaviour: `DrugController1_10Test` calls `conceptService.saveDrug` to seed drugs before checking `strength` in the default and full representations and when creating a drug omod/src/test/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/controller/openmrs1_10/DrugController1_10Test.java. These are the tests most likely to break if the save behaviour (audit fields, returned object, validation) changes.",
          "citations": [
            4,
            5,
            6,
            7,
            8,
            9,
            10,
            11,
            12
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Likely but not directly verified**",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- Any class extending `MetadataDelegatingCrudResource<Drug>` or calling the inherited `save()` would route into the same code, but in this module the only `saveDrug` callers are the four files above (grep over the module returns the same 6 hits in 4 files omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/resource/openmrs1_8/DrugResource1_8.java).\n- ESM clients in scope only *read* `/drug` (drug search / drug-by-uuid, e.g. the patient-chart drug search resources and the stock-management drug selector), so they would be affected only indirectly — if a changed save altered the shape or availability of drug data they then fetch. I did not trace an ESM write to `/drug` in these repositories.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Not checked**",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- Repositories outside the selected set, and any module or external client that writes drugs through `/ws/rest/v1/drug`.\n- Reflection/dynamic dispatch paths, and whether a specific behaviour change (e.g. locking, privilege checks in the `@PreAuthorize` on the interface api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/ConceptService.java) would be caught by additional integration tests elsewhere.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "```mermaid\n---\ntitle: Who reaches ConceptService.saveDrug from webservices.rest\n---\nflowchart TD\n  drugRes[\"DrugResource1_8.save()\"] --> saveDrug[\"ConceptService.saveDrug()\"]\n  drugRefMap[\"DrugReferenceMapResource1_10.save()\"] --> saveDrug\n  ingSave[\"DrugIngredientResource1_11.save()\"] --> saveDrug\n  ingPurge[\"DrugIngredientResource1_11.purge()\"] --> saveDrug\n  saveDrug --> impl[\"ConceptServiceImpl.saveDrug(): lock check, delegate\"]\n  impl --> dao[\"HibernateConceptDAO.saveDrug(): saveOrUpdate\"]\n  subgraph clients[\"REST clients\"]\n    restGet[\"GET /ws/rest/v1/drug\"]\n    restPost[\"POST/PUT /ws/rest/v1/drug\"]\n  end\n  restPost --> drugRes\n  restGet --> drugRes\n```",
          "citations": []
        }
      ],
